course: dictionary
lesson: 15823
title: One word, three meanings: uncovered
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning, and uncovered has three. Read the words around it to find which meaning fits. «The rain fell on the uncovered pot.» Here uncovered means open, with no lid or cover on it.
explain: Uncovered is also the past form of uncover, which means to take the cover off. «Sam uncovered the cake and smelled the chocolate.» Sam took the cover off, so uncovered is the action in the past.
explain: The third meaning is found or discovered something hidden. «The detectives uncovered the truth at last.» Ask yourself: what was hidden before? The truth was hidden, so uncovered means it was found out. Try your meaning in the sentence to check it makes sense.
fact: Uncovered means not covered, open or bare.
fact: Uncovered is the past form of uncover, which means took the cover off.
fact: Uncovered can also mean found or discovered something hidden: «Archaeologists uncovered old bones in the field.»
fact: In maths, uncovered can mean the part that is not covered: the area of the floor minus the area of the rug.
fact: Uncovered food can attract flies, so keep food covered.
exercise: «The uncovered pot was left on the table all night.» What does uncovered mean here? | Found by a detective | Hidden under a cloth | Cooked and eaten | *Open, with no lid
exercise: «Mum uncovered the plate, and the smell of toast filled the kitchen.» Which meaning does uncovered have here? | Broke into pieces | Found something hidden | Not covered, bare | *Took the cover off, the past of uncover
exercise: «The detective uncovered the truth.» What does uncovered mean? | Painted in bright colours | *Found or discovered something hidden | Open, with no lid | Stolen from a shop
test: «The floor has 20 squares, and the rug covers 12. The uncovered part is 8 squares.» What does uncovered mean in this maths sum? | Hidden under a cloth | *The part of the floor that is not covered, 8 squares | Bigger than the rug | Covered by the rug
test: Which sentence uses uncovered to mean found something hidden? | The bread was left uncovered on the bench | The bottle top was uncovered and left out | The lamp is uncovered and open to the air | *The scientists uncovered a buried coin in the garden
exam: Read «The cat sat on the uncovered wall.» Which meaning fits, and why? | Found something hidden, because the cat was hiding | Cooked and eaten, because the cat was hungry | *Not covered, open and bare, because nothing is over the wall | Took the cover off, because the cat removed a lid
